# sum_of_divisors:
# CSES 1082, Sum of Divisors (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1082), in our own
# words: for each i from 1 to n, add up the positive integers that divide i, and
# add those totals up for all i, modulo 10^9 + 7. The input is a binary natural
# (corpora/library/binary/natural) n >= 1, and the answer a binary natural. Part of
# the CSES port's third batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: for each i, the divisors are
# found by trying every number d from 1 to i and keeping those with i mod d = 0, and their
# sum is added to a running total over the i; the total is reduced modulo
# 10^9 + 7. The reading takes about n^2 / 2 divisions; the replacement the family asks
# for is the sum over d of d times floor(n / d), which is constant over runs of d where
# floor(n / d) does not change, so about the square root of n runs, summed in closed
# form, on fixed-width integers modulo 10^9 + 7.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application
# only: its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal (the modulus
# and the numerals are written with binary_zero, binary_even and binary_odd). It
# β-reduces to V, the canonical binary numeral of the answer: every recursion
# ends, since the walk over the divisors consumes the bounded gap i - d, the walk over
# the numbers consumes the bounded gap n - i, and binary_modulo consumes the bits of
# its number; the branches that a Scott boolean discards are never read.
# ../common/binary_modular's binary_modulo, which writes no top, is called with
# d >= 1 and with the positive modulus only. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the soundness of the derivable
# equations for the contextual preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W,
# while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to
# λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the
# second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero binary_even binary_odd _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment merge_binary_plus _ merge_binary_equality
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "cses") "common") "binary_modular")
λ _ _ _ binary_modulo
. (λtuple. tuple λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd binary_zero)
λ modulus
. (λtuple. tuple (binary_odd binary_zero))
λ one
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ number
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self divisor sum
        . binary_less_than number divisor sum (self (merge_binary_increment divisor) (merge_binary_equality (binary_modulo number divisor) binary_zero (merge_binary_plus sum divisor) sum))
      ) one binary_zero
  )
λ divisor_sum
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ limit
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self number sum
        . binary_less_than limit number sum (self (merge_binary_increment number) (merge_binary_plus sum (divisor_sum number)))
      ) one binary_zero
  )
λ total_of_divisor_sums
. (λtuple. tuple λlimit. binary_modulo (total_of_divisor_sums limit) modulus)
λ sum_of_divisors
. export sum_of_divisors
